I. Check your CLISP

You should have CLISP installed. The necessary version is
2.39 of 2006-07-16 or a newer one.

At the terminal window, try to issue the command
  clisp
  
If CLISP starts, issue the command:
  (lisp-implementation-version)
The result should be like this:    
  [1]> (lisp-implementation-version)
  "2.39 (2006-07-16) (built on stnt067 [192.168.0.1])"
  [2]>_

Then enter
  (quit)
to terminate the CLISP session.  

If CLISP does not start, ask you system administrator to get 
the newest CLISP from 
  http://clisp.sourceforge.net/ 
and to install it globally for all users.

II. Automatic installation

If CLISP is installed and the version is new enough, change to 
the directory <bergman-root-dir>/scripts/clisp/unix and issue a command:
  ./mkbergman -auto
for an automatic installation.

If you issue a command
  ./mkbergman -auto -i
you will be informed on each automatically found installation
parameter and can change its value at necessity. (-i is for
interaction.)

III. Manual installation

The manual installation is used mainly by developers in non-standard
situations.

The syntax of the installation command is:
  ./mkbergman <clisp-dir> <bergman-root-dir> <lisp-executable-file-name>
and you can omit the 3rd parameter, or the 2nd and the 3rd parameters. 
Omitted parameters will be found automatically.

To find <clisp-dir> and <lisp-executable-file-name>, issue the command:
  which clisp
You will see something like:
  /usr/local/bin/clisp
Then 
  <clisp-dir> = /usr/local/bin
  <lisp-executable-file-name> = clisp

IV. Log file

  Log of installation is <bergman-root-dir>/logs/clunix.log.  